\date{2025-11-10T03:54:06Z}
\title{Typing rules for delay}

\import{swarm-macros}

\p{The rules for delay types are straightforward:

\rules{
  \inferrule
    {\swty{\Gamma}{t}{\tau}{\Delta}}
    {\swty{\Gamma}{\app{\sf{delay}}{t}}{\Delay{\Delta}{\tau}}{\varnothing}}
}

\rules{
  \inferrule
    {\swty{\Gamma}{t}{\Delay{\Delta_1}{\tau}}{\Delta_2}}
    {\swty{\Gamma}{\app{\sf{force}}{t}}{\tau}{\Delta_1 \cup \Delta_2}}
}

If we wrap a term in a delay, then any capabilities needed to evaluate it are put off until such time as its evaluation is forced.

}